module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.store_refusal_reported_as_contention

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data store_refusal_reported_as_contention: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "store_refusal_reported_as_contention" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a conditional-write realization reports every unsuccessful write as a lost precondition, without observing that a competing publication actually defeated the expectation. HARM: permission, capacity, or IO refusal becomes ordinary contention; the caller re-evaluates and retries against a phantom winner while the operational deficit disappears from its own refusal channel. This is the DESIGN section 5 refusal-as-contention widen, not a missing shared outcome.",

    "SPECIMEN: gunbc.durable_cas_file_store cas_commit_at maps every unsuccessful extdeps.filesystem.filesystem_io Filesystem.WriteOwnerOnly to std.durable_compare_and_set CasPreconditionFailed. Its re-observation may still satisfy the original expectation. The shared CasStoreRefused arm already exists, so an SCM-local outcome sum would duplicate an authority instead of repairing this realization. gunbc.fabric_control_plane consumes file_compare_and_set today; the defect is live for compute control-plane operations. No SCM caller reaches it yet because no SCM conditional-publication caller exists, not because the realization is safe for that consumer.",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACT: cas_probe_as_readable deliberately documents its ProbedBeyondBound-to-CasReadableAbsent projection for reporting a lost race. The defect is cas_commit_at consuming that projection to construct a decision payload without first establishing a race; the vehicle is the bound collapse, the class is refusal-as-contention. observe_cas_slot_state already preserves the bound as CasUnreadableMalformed. Separately cas_probe_from treats unsuccessful reads as chain end even though Filesystem.Read now carries error_kind and filesystem_exact_read can distinguish absence from unreadability. Neither lost observation establishes an empty slot.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: the affected refusal class is silent wrongness, outside the ladder; discovery by source inspection is not executed prevention. These are SOURCE-VERIFIED readings of a contract mismatch, not executed reproductions. No new wet evidence is claimed by this row. CEILING: mechanically preventable at the external store boundary, because filesystem success, availability, and durable visibility must be observed rather than made true by a native constructor. The internal readable-versus-unreadable partition can climb by construction, but cannot establish the external observation itself.",

    "NEXT TRIGGER: the existing file-store realization consumes typed host read/write failure classification, preserves unreadable and bound refusals through CasStoreRefused, and emits CasPreconditionFailed only from an observed violated expectation, with executing required-path evidence distinguishing real contention from operational failure and an accepted successful publication control. A new type, a ticket merge, or a read-back validator alone is insufficient. This repair follows contractual exclusive, complete, durable publication in the Phase 1 SCM consumer cut recorded in docs/plans/native-scm-cas-fit-and-consumer-cut.md; Phase 0 records it and does not implement it.",

    "CONSUMPTION: the derived gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.roster recurring_failure_mode_roster includes this per-class declaration; gunbc.design_ledgers consumes the roster for the on-demand ledger projection, and the required parse-phase rostered-row join checks enrollment. This row is a discovery record, not a CAS witness and not a claim that the defect has been repaired.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
